# ============================================================
# Source assets — too large for git, live outside the repo.
# Encoded/optimized derivatives live in public/hero/ and ARE committed.
# Pipeline: scripts/build-hero-video.sh + scripts/build-hero-image.mjs
# ============================================================
Context/videos/
Context/pictures/
Context/Pics Social Media/
Context/og images/
# Playbook/Guidebook source photos (2026-08-03). CLAUDE.md has described this
# directory as gitignored since the 2026-07-20 build, but no rule ever matched
# it — `git status` listed it as plain untracked, so a stray `git add -A` would
# have committed real photographs of the team to a PUBLIC repo. Same
# encoded-derivatives-are-committed pattern as the entries above: the served
# files live in public/playbook/ and ARE committed (a fresh clone renders fine
# but can't re-encode). Pipeline: scripts/build-playbook-images.mjs
Context/Playbook and guidebook photos/


.vercel

# Claude Code runtime state — local-only, should never be committed
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/*.lock

# Claude Code worktree sandboxes — sibling git workspaces under .claude/.
# These are local-only; tracking them as gitlinks (which `git add -A`
# auto-converts subdirs containing .git into) makes the parent repo
# think they're submodules and creates phantom "modified" entries on
# every status. Always ignored.
.claude/worktrees/

# Local scratch — ad-hoc API dumps made while debugging (e.g. curl of
# /api/products/bookable). Regenerable; never commit. Keeps `git status` clean
# and makes a stray `git add -A` safe.
*_tmp.json

# Windows folder metadata — Explorer drops these into any folder it customizes.
# Would otherwise be committed and served publicly out of public/.
desktop.ini
